 the opt-in: a subscription without one receives no membership events. Every member present narrows the selection (members are ANDed; values within one member are ORed); an empty object selects every membership event the requester is entitled to see.","properties":{"dids":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":100,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Vid"},"description":"Only events whose `principal` or `member` is one of these accounts."},"changes":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/MembershipChange"}},"wires":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/MuxWire"}},"sources":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/MuxSource"}}}},"MembershipChange":{"title":"MembershipChange","type":"string","enum":["attached","detached"],"description":"What happened to a member DID\'s place on a mux connection, as messaging/mux/event reports it to the connection\'s principal. `attached`: the member joined the connection, or its scope or expiry there changed. `detached`: the member left the connection, or a stored grant of it was not attached on connect."},"MuxSource":{"title":"MuxSource","type":"string","enum":["grant","attach"],"description":"How a member came to be on a connection: through a stored grant, or through a session attach bound to that connection."},"MuxWire":{"title":"MuxWire","type":"string","enum":["didcomm","tsp"],"description":"The wire a mux connection speaks: `didcomm`, a DIDComm WebSocket that negotiated the `didcomm-mux` subprotocol; `tsp`, a raw-TSP WebSocket that negotiated `tsp-mux`. The same values messaging/mux/connections reports for a connection\'s `wire`."},"Vid":{"title":"Vid","type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"A Verifiable Identifier (SPEC §4.8). For a mediator-served account this is the account\'s controlling DID, carried verbatim and compared by exact string equality. For privacy — and because some mediators key accounts by a one-way hash and never hold the full DID — a stable hash of the DID (e.g. its SHA-256 digest) is an equally valid value here: producer and consumer simply agree on the same opaque identifier and compare by exact string equality. The field carries whichever form the issuing mediator uses."},"MonitorFilter":{"title":"MonitorFilter","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"description":"Selects which events a monitor subscription receives. Every member present narrows the selection (members are ANDed; values within one member are ORed). An empty filter selects everything the requester is entitled to see.","properties":{"dids":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":100,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Vid"},"description":"Only events whose `from` or `to` is one of these accounts."},"directions":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/TrafficDirection"}},"stages":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/TrafficStage"}},"protocols":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/WireProtocol"}},"channels":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/TrafficChannel"}},"messageTypePrefixes":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":20,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":512},"description":"Only events whose `messageType` starts with one of these strings. Events with no `messageType` never match when this member is present."},"failuresOnly":{"type":"boolean","description":"Only events that carry an `outcome`."}}},"TrafficChannel":{"title":"TrafficChannel","type":"string","enum":["websocket","rest","peerMediator","internal"],"description":"How the traffic reached or left the mediator. `peerMediator` is mediator-to-mediator forwarding."},"WireProtocol":{"title":"WireProtocol","type":"string","enum":["didcomm","didcommV1","tsp","other"],"description":"The protocol a message travelled in, as the mediator detected it from the wire form. `didcomm` is DIDComm v2 (JWE/JWS); `didcommV1` is a DIDComm v1 envelope; `tsp` is a Trust Spanning Protocol message; `other` is anything the mediator could not classify."},"TrafficStage":{"title":"TrafficStage","type":"string","enum":["received","stored","delivered","forwarded","refused","deleted","expired","purged"],"description":"What happened. `received`: a frame arrived. `stored`: it was queued for a local account. `delivered`: handed to its recipient. `forwarded`: relayed to another mediator. `refused`: rejected (see the event\'s `outcome`). `deleted`: removed by its recipient or an administrator. `expired`: removed by expiry. `purged`: removed by a queue purge."},"TrafficDirection":{"title":"TrafficDirection","type":"string","enum":["inbound","outbound","internal"],"description":"`inbound`: arriving at the mediator. `outbound`: leaving it (delivery to a recipient, or a forward to another mediator). `internal`: a state change with no wire traffic (expiry, deletion, purge)."}}}';

